No flush after every buffer of input (aZ, 22.11.2026; found by the review of that
day). The filter took what ZSTD_compressStream() returns, a hint of the size of the
next input and never 0, for data left to flush, and called ZSTD_flushStream() after
every buffer it compressed: each buffer of input ended a block of zstd, and the
smaller the buffers, the worse the compression. A page of 255 KB at level 3 was 65414
bytes from a file (buffers of 32 KB), 68613 proxied and 77936 through sub_filter,
where zstd -3 of the file gives 64663; a page of 134 KB of lines alike was 59743
bytes through sub_filter, 2960 from a file. Now ZSTD_compressStream2() with
ZSTD_e_continue, whose return is the data left to flush, and a flush only where a
buffer asks for one (proxy_buffering off, ngx.flush()) or the response ends, as the
gzip filter: the data stays with zstd until a block of it is full. The first page:
65209 from a file and proxied, 64657 through sub_filter; the other 2785 through
sub_filter. And the end of the response before a flush where a buffer has both: the
filter flushed and never ended the frame.
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_zstd after extra-patch-zstd-static, -p0.

